    "Original TextInput five-argument mode1 call maps to pinned six-argument provider with explicit kFirst capitalization. Null root preserves actual assertion followed by release no-op. Native text-start observation projects to zero modal creation for null root while true result remains. No original Core text editor behavior equivalence claim.",
    "Actual provider modal editor created and canceled through TextInput::stop; actual RootView removes and deletes modal. No Standard.TextEditor skin descriptor installed, so editor is real empty container; keyboard widgets and rendered prompt are not observed. Original prompt pointer, null callback, mode1 and getParameter order observed at native boundary.",
    "Test derived Pot observes root/frame virtual dispatch; NumericParam is actual CCL with test isEnabled observation. Root overrides count calls and delegate actual focus. Boundary object memory offsets are oracle-only. Concurrency, OOM, invalid parameters, hardware and original binary interoperability excluded.",
    "Historical regression fixture outputs retained unchanged. Historical tests freshly compile new PotControl.cpp before physical existing libpresonus_uc.a; unrelated archive objects are compatibility dependencies. Root retains canonical Linux/full CTest, role/install/compile-once, current-source and guarded admission gates."
